From 4e3dfef68692f47e9ebc2cf39cd5a0b64064bacb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:07:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): PR #1820 nits: hub-admin lookbehind, list
 requires on home route, report home denies [daveey]

Follow-up to review 5885349086 on PR #1820 (claim-gate-refused hub denies stay home).

- kanban_placement_coordination._HUB_ADMIN: use the same (?<![\w/.-]) lookbehind as _HUB, so
  `my-hub-admin '...'` / `hermes-hub-admin '...'` no longer open a hub-write quote (the action inside
  is judged as a bare spelling and stays home).
- kanban_hub_admission_placement.pool_route: the home branch returns the declared requires normalized
  to a list; decision_card_route passes the raw view, so a bare-string requires came back a string.
- Observability for the home route (it overrides a judge deny and spends a hub slot):
  * claim screen: a deny kept home records kept = ACTION_REASON ("needs home coordination action"),
    not the generic "no worker queue fits"; Counts gains home= (a subset of kept) in its log line.
  * pickup._target copies hub_admission.home into the recorded verdict; pickup's skip reason says
    "kept home (<reason>)" instead of "no worker queue fits".
  * describe() (`hermes kanban show` hub: line, kanban_show tool) appends "; kept home: <reason>".

Tests: lookalike prefixes stay home while plain hub-admin still needs hub-write; pool_route home
branch normalizes str/tuple/list/None requires; decision card with string requires; claim-time
home deny records kept/home and the home=1 count; describe line. RED before, GREEN after.
